# Level 49, the same walk as `movies/level49-bubble.zmv` with the B press taken
# out -- so the shots start out as the ordinary $5C.
#
# **They do not stay that way, and that is the finding.** With Y held for
# eighteen hundred frames the squirt gun runs dry, and the game then moves the
# selection on by itself: `weapon_select_next` is called twice on this movie with
# `weapon_changed` both times and no B press anywhere in the file, and
# `--records` shows every shot reading $5C up to about frame 4550 and $5E from
# 4560. So this is not the clean control it was written to be -- it is the same
# weapon arriving later, by a route no input had taken before.
#
# Which makes the pair worth keeping for a different reason than the intended
# one. The two movies' censuses differ: `$81:AC92` appears on both (309 declines
# here against 290), so that handler is a finding about the *route* -- level 49's
# north-west corner is somewhere no input had walked. `$81:845E` appears only
# here, 38 declines. And `$81:83C6` is reached only here, three times, because by
# the time this movie is firing $5E the walk has come back to where the $81:AC92
# creature is and the bubble movie's has not.
#
# The bubble movie fires that weapon from frame 3400 and reaches $81:83C6 zero
# times. One input carrying a new weapon *and* a new route cannot say which of
# them bought which census entry, and this project has been wrong in that exact
# shape before -- see the `monster_collide` dispatch that was counted for four
# rounds and never named.
#
